# D27 accept-both, SELF-HOST resolver lane: the canonical `^` move sigil as a
# TYPE-ARG SUFFIX (`Vector[int ^]`) — the D35 spelling, sigil AFTER the type.
#
# AXIS CELL: glyph = `^` · position = type-arg suffix inside `[...]` ·
# lanes = Rust gg (C + LLVM), self-host resolver, self-host runtime.
#
# This is a DISTINCT parser predicate from the named-param cell: the type-arg
# suffix is consumed by `skip_ownership_markers`, reached from
# `parse_type_args`. `d27_fmt_emits_caret.gg` also spells this position, but
# bundles five positions in one program and is wired only to the FORMATTER
# test; this cell isolates the type-arg predicate so a regression confined to
# it produces an unambiguous signal on the resolver and runtime lanes.
#
# RED-verified against the PRE-port self-host resolver driver: with the
# type-arg suffix predicate un-ported the parser did not consume the `^`,
# tripped on the `]`, and produced a GARBAGE AST — the function body escaped
# to top level (`sum` surfaced as a `DEF Static`) and a `DEF Variable ""`
# appeared, leaving only 2 `RES` lines. Post-port all DEFs carry their names
# and the full set of `RES` edges is produced.
#
# The `!` (retired-glyph) control for this position is the existing corpus;
# no new `!` site is added (`fmt_no_new_move_bang_in_migrated_corpora` in
# tests/lints.rs is shrink-only and at zero headroom).
#
# Expected stdout: 9

int take_owned(Vector[int ^] items):
    int sum = 0
    for v in items:
        sum = sum + v
    return sum

void main():
    Vector[int] xs = Vector[int]()
    xs.push(4)
    xs.push(5)
    print(take_owned(xs))
